WEBVTT

00:01:30.810 --> 00:01:34.900
Schools sure start late these days.

00:01:34.900 --> 00:01:37.490
Today is a school holiday, Madam.

00:01:37.490 --> 00:01:39.570
Isn't that right, young lady?

00:01:40.310 --> 00:01:45.250
My, fancy me not knowing these things.  Some foster-mother I am.

00:01:45.250 --> 00:01:47.920
No!  Not at all!

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:52.460
By the way, Chizuko-san, why don't you accompany me on a trip sometime?

00:01:53.260 --> 00:01:59.130
It's getting nice and green out.  Let's go breathe in some good, fresh air.  Maybe next week.

00:02:00.410 --> 00:02:01.720
No thank you.

00:02:01.720 --> 00:02:03.220
Chizuko-san...

00:02:03.220 --> 00:02:04.810
I have to be going out.

00:02:05.510 --> 00:02:06.790
Please excuse me.

00:02:06.790 --> 00:02:09.230
Ah, I'll help you get ready.

00:02:11.270 --> 00:02:15.050
My, my, my, my, my!  Are you going to a friend's house?

00:02:15.050 --> 00:02:16.260
Y-Yeah.

00:02:16.260 --> 00:02:19.320
Oh, my!  Wait just a second, OK?

00:02:19.320 --> 00:02:21.590
You need to bring a gift!  A gift!

00:02:24.450 --> 00:02:27.630
She wasn't interested in the least.  What a detestable girl.

00:02:27.630 --> 00:02:29.650
An accidental death while on vacation.

00:02:29.650 --> 00:02:32.420
It would've been a perfect opportunity.

00:02:32.420 --> 00:02:38.100
The company that manages all of the Mikamo family assets is going to transfer most of the rights into her hands.

00:02:39.520 --> 00:02:47.140
Thanks for seeing that a formal heir was never named and that the only blood relative, your husband, passed away.

00:02:47.140 --> 00:02:51.650
It was a bit early for him, to be honest.

00:02:51.650 --> 00:02:58.650
But never in my wildest dreams did I imagine she'd come back still alive after being abducted by Twenty Faces.

00:02:58.650 --> 00:02:59.750
That's certainly true.

00:03:01.150 --> 00:03:04.410
Let's think of another way.

00:03:14.430 --> 00:03:18.560
My, my, you brought such large gifts.  So polite!

00:03:18.560 --> 00:03:20.090
I can't thank you enough.

00:03:23.810 --> 00:03:27.400
You're not used to visiting friends, are you?

00:03:28.760 --> 00:03:34.210
Actually, this is the first time Miss Shunka has ever had a friend over!

00:03:41.190 --> 00:03:44.400
So this is what other girls' rooms look like.

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:49.160
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:03:50.540 --> 00:03:52.660
What did you want to show me?

00:03:54.920 --> 00:03:57.460
The true identity of Twenty Faces.

00:04:04.090 --> 00:04:08.560
These are pictures of actors that my mother collected.

00:04:08.560 --> 00:04:10.890
Here, look at this picture.

00:04:11.810 --> 00:04:15.520
This is Namikawa Koheiji, a star actor from the Tenkaiza theater.

00:04:15.520 --> 00:04:18.440
He's performed flawlessly as everything from old men to women.

00:04:18.440 --> 00:04:21.820
Apparently they called him the "Man with Seven Faces".

00:04:23.490 --> 00:04:24.780
Hey, are you listening?

00:04:24.780 --> 00:04:26.490
Y-Yeah.

00:04:26.490 --> 00:04:31.330
So, apparently this Koheiji-san person went missing after the war.

00:04:31.330 --> 00:04:34.410
He looks a little bit like him.

00:04:34.410 --> 00:04:37.830
Want to go?  To the Tenkaiza theater?

00:04:37.830 --> 00:04:40.050
Why would we be looking for him?

00:04:42.090 --> 00:04:43.920
I've...

00:04:43.920 --> 00:04:47.220
...fallen in love.  With Twenty Faces.

00:04:48.220 --> 00:04:52.890
I understand that I'm journeying into a dangerous world by seeking him out.

00:04:54.020 --> 00:04:58.060
But I, Chizuko, long to be together with him!

00:04:58.060 --> 00:05:00.820
S-Stop that, Koito-san!

00:05:06.660 --> 00:05:08.280
I knew it!

00:05:08.820 --> 00:05:11.790
You're in love with Twenty Faces.

00:05:11.790 --> 00:05:13.750
Th-That's not true!

00:05:13.750 --> 00:05:18.630
Seeing you so flustered is all the proof I need.  It's just as I thought.

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:21.340
I told you, it's not like–

00:05:21.340 --> 00:05:25.630
Twenty Faces, the man who stole your heart and passed away.

00:05:25.630 --> 00:05:28.760
We're going to follow the path that he trod.

00:05:28.760 --> 00:05:30.930
There's no way he's dead!

00:05:30.930 --> 00:05:33.560
See?  You really believe that, don't you?

00:05:33.560 --> 00:05:35.430
That's why we have to search for him.

00:05:35.430 --> 00:05:38.440
OK?  OK?  Let's go look!

00:05:45.360 --> 00:05:47.740
All right, that's the last of it.

00:05:47.740 --> 00:05:50.450
Ah, so boring!  Ah, so boring!

00:05:50.450 --> 00:05:54.410
These are our seven tools of the trade.  We're going to form the Detective Girls.

00:05:54.410 --> 00:05:56.290
Detective Girls?

00:05:56.290 --> 00:05:59.250
Exactly.  Searching for someone who has gone missing.

00:05:59.250 --> 00:06:01.630
It's a splendid job for a detective!

00:06:03.960 --> 00:06:07.170
Then from this moment forth, you're a detective.

00:06:09.180 --> 00:06:10.840
Is something the matter?

00:06:10.840 --> 00:06:14.600
Nope.  By the way, what is all this?

00:06:14.600 --> 00:06:15.720
A radio.

00:06:15.720 --> 00:06:17.600
Some rubber to tie up bad guys.

00:06:17.600 --> 00:06:20.100
Tiddlywinks to help us retrace our path.

00:06:20.100 --> 00:06:21.230
A hand-mirror.

00:06:21.230 --> 00:06:23.360
And this here is...

00:06:23.360 --> 00:06:25.320
A disguise, right?

00:06:25.320 --> 00:06:26.490
Precisely!

00:06:26.490 --> 00:06:29.530
You should take some of them too, Mikamo-san.

00:06:29.530 --> 00:06:30.610
Sure.

00:06:30.610 --> 00:06:33.330
I'm bored out of my mind.

00:06:33.330 --> 00:06:35.370
That's Pippo, my carrier pigeon.

00:06:35.370 --> 00:06:37.000
Kyuu-chan!  Good morning.

00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:37.910
Kyuu-chan!

00:06:37.910 --> 00:06:39.000
A pigeon...

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:42.170
No!  From today on, you're Pippo.

00:06:42.170 --> 00:06:45.000
OK, Pippo?  Let's hear you say your name.

00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:46.590
You're Pippo.

00:06:46.590 --> 00:06:47.840
Kyuu-chan!

00:06:47.840 --> 00:06:49.630
No!  It's Pippo!

00:06:49.630 --> 00:06:50.510
Kyuu-chan!

00:06:50.510 --> 00:06:53.140
Damn it!  Say Pippo already!

00:06:53.140 --> 00:06:54.810
Kyuu-chan!

00:06:54.810 --> 00:06:56.390
We're heading out!

00:06:57.180 --> 00:06:59.350
We'll be back before supper.

00:07:00.230 --> 00:07:02.850
Take good care of yourselves.

00:07:02.850 --> 00:07:06.110
My nanny is such a worrywart.

00:07:09.650 --> 00:07:12.740
What's wrong?  You'll miss the train.

00:07:13.990 --> 00:07:15.280
Right.

00:07:36.510 --> 00:07:39.020
I can't believe there'd be a well here.

00:07:43.690 --> 00:07:47.070
Wow, such clear water.  This is great!

00:07:53.820 --> 00:07:57.120
Anything can be a clue.  Ready to go?

00:07:57.120 --> 00:07:58.120
Yeah.

00:08:00.500 --> 00:08:02.910
These paper candies...

00:08:02.910 --> 00:08:06.170
These things are impossible to bite through.

00:08:06.170 --> 00:08:07.420
Yeah.

00:08:07.420 --> 00:08:10.670
You need to chew them like this to get to the flavor.

00:08:13.680 --> 00:08:16.390
W-We knew that!

00:08:16.390 --> 00:08:18.430
Right, Mikamo-san?

00:08:19.560 --> 00:08:21.560
W-Wow.

00:08:22.310 --> 00:08:23.520
Wow.

00:08:25.480 --> 00:08:26.860
Looks like I win.

00:08:26.860 --> 00:08:27.730
Darn it.

00:08:27.730 --> 00:08:29.860
Look at these, Mikamo-san.

00:08:32.740 --> 00:08:34.110
They're pretty.

00:08:34.110 --> 00:08:36.160
Half of these are yours.

00:08:43.410 --> 00:08:44.540
Thank you.

00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:48.000
OK, let's get going.

00:08:48.000 --> 00:08:48.670
Yeah.

00:08:50.840 --> 00:08:53.220
Good-bye.  Thanks for everything.

00:08:53.220 --> 00:08:56.380
Yeah.  See you later, Oneechan!

00:08:59.970 --> 00:09:04.430
Sign:  Tenkaiza Hall

00:09:04.640 --> 00:09:07.270
So that's Koheiji.

00:09:07.270 --> 00:09:10.820
I heard that attendance is way down ever since he disappeared.

00:09:12.280 --> 00:09:14.280
Koheiji is dead.

00:09:16.530 --> 00:09:18.410
Koheiji is...

00:09:18.410 --> 00:09:19.450
...gone.

00:09:32.500 --> 00:09:35.470
Excuse me, can you tell us about Koheiji-san?

00:09:38.680 --> 00:09:42.180
You girls there!  Can we help you with something?

00:09:44.060 --> 00:09:49.440
This is second-hand information, but apparently Koheiji returned here once after the war ended.

00:09:49.440 --> 00:09:52.610
"I'll never get up on stage again."

00:09:52.610 --> 00:09:55.940
With those parting words, he vanished.

00:09:55.940 --> 00:09:59.490
But the old man said that Koheiji-san had died.

00:09:59.490 --> 00:10:02.700
That geezer doesn't know what the heck he's talking about.

00:10:02.700 --> 00:10:07.710
He's completely worthless but the troupe leader takes care of him for some reason.

00:10:07.710 --> 00:10:10.170
Hey!  What are you just standing around for?!

00:10:10.170 --> 00:10:12.210
Ah, crap.

00:10:12.210 --> 00:10:14.420
Go get the stage prepped!

00:10:14.420 --> 00:10:18.170
Th-These two girls were asking about Koheiji.

00:10:18.170 --> 00:10:20.220
Please take it from here, sir.

00:10:21.510 --> 00:10:22.760
Watch out!

00:10:25.640 --> 00:10:27.100
Keep going!

00:10:27.100 --> 00:10:30.190
I'll be killed if I fall!

00:10:30.190 --> 00:10:33.110
No!  I can't dishonor my men!

00:10:33.110 --> 00:10:35.230
No!  I must march on!

00:10:35.230 --> 00:10:37.690
It's all right.  This is a playhouse.

00:10:37.690 --> 00:10:39.030
You have nothing to worry about.

00:10:39.030 --> 00:10:41.360
Kill me!  Kill me now!

00:10:41.360 --> 00:10:43.030
I won't join your P.O.W. camp!

00:10:43.030 --> 00:10:45.090
Calm down.  I'm here with you.

00:10:45.090 --> 00:10:47.160
It's fine.  Everything's fine.

00:10:47.160 --> 00:10:48.910
This is Tenkaiza.

00:10:56.090 --> 00:10:58.090
Koheiji-san?

00:11:02.090 --> 00:11:04.100
Koheiji is...

00:11:04.100 --> 00:11:05.060
...gone.

00:11:06.970 --> 00:11:09.230
Koheiji is dead.

00:11:14.770 --> 00:11:20.030
That's right.  That's the man who used to be the master of the stage, Namikawa Koheiji.

00:11:21.110 --> 00:11:22.200
Hold on a second.

00:11:22.990 --> 00:11:25.830
He should only be in his 30's.

00:11:27.910 --> 00:11:31.080
Where will I go tomorrow?

00:11:32.790 --> 00:11:35.590
The war killed Koheiji the actor.

00:11:35.840 --> 00:11:37.960
I don't know what happened out on that battlefield,

00:11:37.960 --> 00:11:43.510
but whenever he hears a loud noise it pulls him right back into the war.

00:11:43.510 --> 00:11:47.260
The war changed everything.

00:11:49.270 --> 00:11:52.850
The fact that Tenkaiza is even here today is all thanks to him.

00:11:53.270 --> 00:11:56.770
Now it's my turn to take care of him!

00:12:00.780 --> 00:12:06.280
Man, I really thought he'd be Twenty Faces.

00:12:09.700 --> 00:12:13.790
Hey, no need to get so depressed just 'cause we were a bit disappointed.

00:12:14.460 --> 00:12:15.960
The war...

00:12:15.960 --> 00:12:18.170
Hey, are you listening?

00:12:23.340 --> 00:12:24.130
What is it?

00:12:24.130 --> 00:12:25.340
We're being followed.

00:12:25.340 --> 00:12:27.300
Koito-san, run and get away.

00:12:27.300 --> 00:12:29.310
Who is it?  An evil organization?

00:12:29.310 --> 00:12:32.060
Nothing that exciting.

00:12:35.520 --> 00:12:39.230
So?  Which one of you is the daughter of Twenty Faces?

00:12:39.770 --> 00:12:42.030
That'd be me.  What's it to you?

00:12:42.030 --> 00:12:43.700
H-Hey...

00:12:44.450 --> 00:12:46.610
Where's that legacy and stuff?

00:12:46.610 --> 00:12:49.120
She has nothing to do with that.  I'm–

00:12:49.120 --> 00:12:51.240
Be quiet, you impostor.

00:12:51.240 --> 00:12:53.620
Which one's the real one, bro?

00:12:53.620 --> 00:12:56.830
Who cares?  We'll take both of them together.

00:12:58.710 --> 00:12:59.960
Here we come!

00:12:59.960 --> 00:13:01.130
Stop that!

00:13:01.130 --> 00:13:01.250
Ouch!

00:13:02.960 --> 00:13:04.340
Y-You jerk!

00:13:09.680 --> 00:13:11.180
You think you're funny?!

00:13:11.680 --> 00:13:13.020
My turn!

00:13:15.350 --> 00:13:16.440
Sorry!

00:13:16.440 --> 00:13:18.690
Heh.  I'll get this one.

00:13:26.450 --> 00:13:31.330
Wow, I guess that's why they call you the daughter of Twenty Faces.

00:13:32.870 --> 00:13:36.870
So what's more important to you, your schoolmate's life or the legacy?

00:13:37.750 --> 00:13:40.540
I'll cut out this liar's tongue.

00:13:40.540 --> 00:13:42.590
M-Mikamo-san...

00:13:48.130 --> 00:13:50.090
Very well.

00:13:50.090 --> 00:13:52.100
I'll give you the map to the treasure.

00:14:03.780 --> 00:14:06.780
Awesome!  You're making good use of the tools.

00:14:06.780 --> 00:14:08.950
Damn it.  Don't screw around with me!

00:14:13.990 --> 00:14:14.910
Hurry!

00:14:16.290 --> 00:14:18.000
Son of a...

00:14:19.290 --> 00:14:21.040
Geez, he's persistent.

00:14:32.600 --> 00:14:35.060
I told you the seven tools of the trade would come in handy.

00:14:35.060 --> 00:14:36.220
You're right.

00:14:37.100 --> 00:14:39.810
Detective Girls, our mission is completed.

00:15:24.610 --> 00:15:28.400
Take that girl and the fatty to the hospital.

00:15:28.400 --> 00:15:30.740
We'll take their statements afterwards.

00:15:31.740 --> 00:15:32.990
Come on.  Get in, get in.

00:15:32.990 --> 00:15:34.320
Ah-ah!  Ah-ah-ah-ah-ah-ah!

00:15:34.320 --> 00:15:36.990
Don't be so pushy.  I'm not injured.

00:15:36.990 --> 00:15:38.450
No, no!

00:15:38.450 --> 00:15:42.040
H-Hey, Chizuko-kun.  Can you talk to them for me?

00:15:48.000 --> 00:15:49.380
Chiko.

00:15:49.380 --> 00:15:50.840
I'm glad she's safe.

00:15:51.420 --> 00:15:53.720
OK, you guys take it from here.

00:16:02.560 --> 00:16:03.600
Boss?

00:16:05.360 --> 00:16:07.980
That was the boss, wasn't it?

00:16:07.980 --> 00:16:10.650
He was watching over her.

00:16:10.650 --> 00:16:12.990
Boss, take good care of Chiko.

00:16:32.090 --> 00:16:33.470
This is it.

00:16:33.470 --> 00:16:35.760
It's supposed to be a really good movie.

00:16:35.760 --> 00:16:36.760
Let's go.

00:17:02.160 --> 00:17:03.830
You're slow, Boss.

00:17:03.830 --> 00:17:05.160
You're slow, Boss.

00:17:05.160 --> 00:17:07.420
How many days has it been?

00:17:07.420 --> 00:17:08.790
Hey, Kai-nii?

00:17:15.930 --> 00:17:17.800
He wouldn't be here.

00:17:23.310 --> 00:17:24.390
Chiko?

00:17:25.310 --> 00:17:26.770
In Japan?

00:17:26.770 --> 00:17:30.270
I can't believe they brought her back to that two-faced family.

00:17:30.650 --> 00:17:31.270
Shit!

00:17:33.990 --> 00:17:36.320
What are you doing, Boss?!

00:17:36.320 --> 00:17:39.530
Why haven't you and Chiko come back?!

00:17:42.490 --> 00:17:45.120
You couldn't have...

00:17:45.120 --> 00:17:47.040
...left me here.

00:17:47.040 --> 00:17:49.290
I don't need you around.

00:17:50.500 --> 00:17:52.920
With you gone, I'd be able to...

00:17:52.920 --> 00:17:53.760
Ma... Mama...

00:17:53.760 --> 00:17:54.630
Ma... Mama...

00:17:54.630 --> 00:17:56.920
With you gone, I'd be able to...

00:18:02.890 --> 00:18:05.220
There's no one here.

00:18:05.220 --> 00:18:06.600
It happened again.

00:18:06.600 --> 00:18:09.900
I was abandoned again.

00:18:13.900 --> 00:18:18.070
Coming this summer, a truly epic film:  Eternal Love.

00:18:18.950 --> 00:18:20.780
Another preview?

00:18:22.280 --> 00:18:28.120
This film is being shot entirely on an uninhabited island in the Sea of Japan.

00:18:28.580 --> 00:18:33.460
The entire staff and cast will be stationed there for a long period of time.  Filming has just begun.

00:18:34.590 --> 00:18:38.130
The film centers around this necklace.

00:18:38.130 --> 00:18:41.260
It contains a radiant gemstone sometimes called the "Fairy of the Night".

00:18:41.260 --> 00:18:45.600
Even if you traversed the entire globe, you'd never find another one like it.

00:18:45.600 --> 00:18:47.520
Twenty Faces had that.

00:18:50.060 --> 00:18:52.520
It's a radiant gemstone that sparkles in the night.

00:18:54.520 --> 00:18:57.780
Men can become lost in its mysterious glow.

00:18:59.030 --> 00:19:02.240
Why is his gemstone in this movie?

00:19:05.450 --> 00:19:07.660
H-Hey.  Where are you going?

00:19:09.460 --> 00:19:11.120
Nagaishi Island, right?

00:19:11.120 --> 00:19:12.920
Thank you very much.

00:19:26.060 --> 00:19:26.930
Hey...

00:19:29.600 --> 00:19:31.690
I apologize for what I said before.

00:19:31.690 --> 00:19:35.610
Is it too late to talk about going on that trip?

00:19:35.610 --> 00:19:37.730
Why the sudden change of heart?

00:19:37.730 --> 00:19:40.150
But this is quite convenient.

00:19:40.150 --> 00:19:41.900
My, I'm so glad to hear that.

00:19:41.900 --> 00:19:44.120
I see you thought it over.

00:19:44.120 --> 00:19:45.660
Yes.

00:19:46.490 --> 00:19:48.240
It'll be a great trip.

00:19:48.240 --> 00:19:49.450
I'm looking forward to it.

00:19:49.450 --> 00:19:51.540
Yeah, me too.

00:19:51.540 --> 00:19:54.500
You've got so many things surrounding you.

00:19:54.500 --> 00:19:56.920
Family, friends.

00:19:59.300 --> 00:20:02.010
Why do you want to go to Nagaishi Island again?

00:20:02.010 --> 00:20:04.800
I want to see a movie shoot.

00:20:04.800 --> 00:20:08.810
I see.  Actually, I know some people at this film studio.

00:20:08.810 --> 00:20:09.890
That's great!

00:20:09.890 --> 00:20:12.310
But, young lady, what about school?

00:20:12.310 --> 00:20:14.310
I'll speak to the headmaster.

00:20:14.310 --> 00:20:16.230
My sincere apologies.

00:20:16.230 --> 00:20:17.610
I shouldn't have been so forward.

00:20:17.610 --> 00:20:20.610
Well now, I'll go reserve our tickets.

00:20:20.610 --> 00:20:22.820
Thank you, Auntie.

00:20:22.820 --> 00:20:25.320
Tome, you should come along as well.

00:20:25.320 --> 00:20:27.160
To look after Chizuko-san.

00:20:27.160 --> 00:20:28.410
What?

00:20:28.410 --> 00:20:30.330
Are you sure?

00:20:40.760 --> 00:20:44.760
You have no idea that this will be the last vacation of your life.

00:20:51.350 --> 00:20:52.730
Young lady...

00:20:59.610 --> 00:21:00.650
Mister...
